# WHY THIS SITS BESIDE 1.4.0 RATHER THAN REPLACING IT
#
# third_party/dsp0274.pin pins 1.4.0 and is NOT retired by this file. Every
# claim in docs/certchain.md and every field name in certs/openssl.cnf was
# checked against the text of 1.4.0, and verify_repo.sh asserts that those two
# files still carry 1.4.0's digest. Moving the pin would leave those claims
# citing a document nobody had read them against — which is the failure standing
# rule 7 describes, arriving through the front door.
#
# So: a pinned document is the evidence that the claims checked against it were
# checked. Replacing it does not update those claims; it un-checks them.
# docs/decisions/0011-two-versions-of-one-specification.md is the long version.
#
# And in this particular case the DIFFERENCE between the two versions is the
# result. DMTF-2026-0003 is a defect in a document, and the only way to show
# it was repaired is to hold both documents open. A single pin cannot express
# a diff.
#
# WHAT WAS CHECKED, AND WHAT IT SAYS
#
# 1.4.0 re-downloaded on the same day as this file and hashed to
# a2035c64f614640ba34133ad255589269bf13c9d816414638fb22d89eb5369d9, which is
# byte for byte the digest third_party/dsp0274.pin recorded on 2026-08-31. The
# pin still names the document it named eight weeks ago.
#
# Extracted with `pdftotext -layout` from both, the phrase
#
#     [FINISH] . SPDM Header Fields      (and [FINISH_RSP] . SPDM Header fields)
#
# occurs FIVE times in 1.4.0 and ZERO times in 1.4.1 — which is the count the
# advisory gives for affected definitions, arrived at independently. All five
# now read "* except the ... field(s)". docs/transcript.md section 3 quotes
# both versions of all five side by side.
#
# 1.4.1 is 313 pages against 1.4.0's 306, and is the SMALLER file (1,670,077
# bytes against 1,838,236) — a different PDF producer, not a smaller document.
# Neither number is evidence of anything and both are here so that a reader who
# downloads it and gets different ones knows immediately.
#
# Not vendored — the PDF is not this repository's to redistribute, and lives
# outside it under LAB_DIR/spec/dsp0274_141.pdf. What is pinned is the digest
# of the exact file that was read.
